.TH WERCFS 4
.SH NAME
wercfs \- a werc site as the files a web server sends
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wercfs
[
.BI -w " wercroot"
]
.I sitedir
.PP
.B mount {wercfs
.IB sitedir }
.I dir
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Wercfs
serves a site laid out for werc
(the rc web framework of
.BR werc.cat-v.org )
as its pages, made: a page's Markdown, HTML or text in werc's
master template, with werc's menu, title and included files.
It is meant to be mounted where
.IR httpd (8)
serves, which runs no programs (there is no CGI) and sends files;
werc is rc run as CGI, and here it is a file server instead.
.PP
.I Sitedir
is the site's directory, as werc has it under
.BI sites/ domain\fR.
.I Wercroot
is werc's own directory, holding
.B lib/
(werc's
.B top_bar.inc
and
.BR footer.inc ),
.B pub/
(its style sheet) and
.B sites/
(where
.B $masterSite
is looked for).
Without
.BR -w ,
it is the directory above
.IR sitedir 's
when that is named
.B sites
and holds a
.BR lib/ ;
otherwise there is none, and only the site's own files are used.
.PP
What is served is read-only, and made when it is looked at: an edit
to the site is seen at the next request.
.SH FILES SERVED
In the site's own terms, from its root:
.TF /_werc/pub/...
.TP
.B /
The site's directory.
Its directories are directories here, and its files are here as they are
.RB ( /foo.md ,
.BR /img.png ).
.TP
.B /index.html
A directory's page:
.BR index.md ,
.B index.html
or
.B index.txt
(the first there is) made as a page is;
with none, werc's listing of the directory in the template, between its
.B _header.md
and
.BR _footer.md .
.I Httpd
sends it for the directory's
.BR / .
.TP
.B /foo
A page, from
.BR foo.md ,
.B foo.html
or
.B foo.txt
(the first there is), as werc's
.B setup_handlers
chooses.
Its name has no extension, as werc's URLs have none: serve the site with
.I httpd
.B "-T text/html"
for pages to be sent as HTML.
.TP
.B /pub/...
The site's
.BR pub/ ,
and for a name it does not have,
.IR wercroot 's
(werc's
.BR pub/style/style.css ,
which its template links).
.TP
.B /_werc/pub/...
The site's own
.BR _werc/pub/ :
its
.BR style.css ,
linked when there is one.
.PD
.PP
Nothing else of a
.B _werc
directory is served: its
.B config
and
.B lib/
are the site's source, not its pages.
Nor is a name beginning with a dot.
A directory and a page of one name are the directory, as in werc;
a page hides a file of its own name.
.PP
.I Wercfs
reads the site as
.I httpd
does: once started it runs in a name space of its own with
.B NODEVS
(see
.IR sys-pctl (2)),
so in the hosted emulator no host symbolic link is followed
.RI ( fs (3)),
and one in the site cannot bring a page, an included file or a file
served as it is from outside it.
.PP
A page is a file of known length, with the time of the newest thing it
was made from and a qid version that is a hash of what it holds, so
.I httpd
gives it a
.BR Content-Length ,
an
.B ETag
that changes when the page does and not otherwise, ranges and
.BR 304 s,
as for any file.
It is kept once made, with the stat of each thing it was made from (its
source, each
.B _werc/config
down its path, the included files, the directories its menu lists),
and made again when one has changed.
.SH PAGES
A page is made as werc 1.5 makes it
.RB ( bin/werc.rc ,
.BR bin/corehandlers.rc ,
.BR lib/headers.tpl ,
.BR lib/default_master.tpl ),
with its elements, ids and classes, so werc's style sheets apply unchanged:
.TP
The body
A
.B .md
through
.IR mdhtml (2)
(Markdown as werc's Markdown.pl formats it: raw HTML passed through);
a
.BR .html 's
contents between
.B <body ...>
and
.B </body>
(or all of it, with none), as werc's
.BR html_handler ;
a
.B .txt
escaped in
.BR <pre> .
.TP
The title
A
.BR .md 's
first line when the second is all
.BR = ,
a
.BR .html 's
.BR <title> ;
otherwise the path's elements joined by
.LR " - " ,
with
.B _
and a
.B -
between letters as blanks
.RB ( /docs/setup-guide
is
.LR "docs - setup guide" );
at the root,
.B $siteTitle
and
.BR $siteSubTitle .
.TP
The menu
werc's
.BR nav_tree :
the root's pages and directories, and each directory's on the path to the
page, nested, sorted, the extension dropped,
.B _
and
.B -
shown as blanks, those on the path marked
.B class="thisPage"
and
.BR &raquo; ;
names beginning with
.B _
or
.BR . ,
the
.B index
pages,
.BR robots.txt ,
.B sitemap.txt
and names matching
.B conf_hide_paths
left out (they are still served),
headed by
.B $sideBarNavTitle
when it is set.
.TP
Included files
.BR top_bar.inc ,
.B footer.inc
and
.BR headers.inc ,
each the first found of the site's
.BR _werc/lib/ ,
.BR $masterSite 's
.RI ( wercroot /sites/ $masterSite /_werc/lib/ )
and
.IR wercroot /lib/ ,
put in as they are, as werc's
.B cat
puts them.
.TP
The head
.BR $meta_description ,
.B $meta_keywords
and
.B $extraHeaders
as werc's
.B headers.tpl
puts them.
.SH CONFIGURATION
A site's
.B _werc/config
files are read as werc sources them: the root's, then each directory's
on the path to the page, a later one overriding an earlier.
They are rc, and
.I wercfs
does not run rc; it takes, of them, plain assignments
.RB ( name=word ,
.BR name='quoted' ,
.BR "name=(a list)" ,
quotes and
.B ''
as rc has them, a
.B #
comment)
and
.B conf_hide_paths
.IR pattern ...
(regular expressions, from the directory of the file naming them, as in
werc).
Every other line is not taken: functions
.RB ( conf_enable_\fIapp\fP ,
.BR conf_perm_redirect ,
.BR ll_add ),
and anything inside braces, whose assignments may not run (an
.B if
or a
.BR switch ).
Each is reported once on standard error, naming the file and line:
.IP
.EX
wercfs: not taken: .../_werc/config:4: conf_enable_comments
.EE
.PP
Werc's variables used are
.BR siteTitle ,
.BR siteSubTitle ,
.BR masterSite ,
.BR meta_description ,
.BR meta_keywords ,
.B extraHeaders
and
.BR sideBarNavTitle .
.SH EXAMPLES
werc's own tree, its site
.B example.org
served on port 80:
.IP
.EX
mount {wercfs /services/werc/sites/example.org} /services/www
svc/httpd/httpd -T text/html /services/www &
.EE
.PP
A site directory alone, werc's style sheet beside it in its
.BR pub/ :
.IP
.EX
mount {wercfs /usr/me/site} /services/www
svc/httpd/httpd -T text/html -c web.pem -k web.key /services/www &
.EE
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/cmd/wercfs.b
.br
.B /appl/lib/mdhtml.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR mdhtml (2),
.IR sys-pctl (2),
.IR fs (3),
.IR httpd (8)
.SH BUGS
Only werc's pages, menu and templates are served.
Werc's apps (blagh's blog, bridge's comments, the dirdir wiki), its
users and logins, the sitemap, and redirects
.RB ( conf_perm_redirect ,
.B /index
to
.BR / )
are not; the apps that take a
.B POST
would need a file to write to, and
.I httpd
has no authentication.
A
.B .tpl
file and a site's own
.B default_master.tpl
are rc, and are not run: the template is werc's default.
.br
werc's 404 page is not used:
.I httpd
answers with its own.
.br
One site to an instance; virtual hosts are one
.I wercfs
and one
.I httpd
each.
